  "question": {
    "text": "If the shortest distance between the lines $\\frac{x-\\lambda}{2}=\\frac{y-4}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{4}$ and $\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{8}$ is $\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{29}}$, then a value of $\\lambda$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iTU6r",
      "text": "-1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "W1xpN",
      "text": "$-\\frac{13}{25}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "mrd9V",
      "text": "$\\frac{13}{25}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wYek2",
      "text": "1",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\left.\\begin{array}{l}\\overline{\\mathrm{r}}_1=(\\lambda \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})+\\alpha(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}) \\\\ \\overline{\\mathrm{r}}_2=(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+7 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})+\\beta(2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}})\\end{array}\\right\\} \\begin{gathered}\\overline{\\mathrm{b}}=2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\ \\overline{\\mathrm{a}}_2+\\lambda \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+3 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}} \\\\ \\mathrm{a}_2=2 \\hat{\\mathrm{i}}+4 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}+7 \\hat{\\mathrm{k}}\\end{gathered}$\nShortest dist. $=\\frac{\\left|\\overline{\\mathrm{b}} \\times\\left(\\overline{\\mathrm{a}}_2-\\overline{\\mathrm{a}}_1\\right)\\right|}{|\\mathrm{b}|}=\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{29}}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\left\\lvert\\, \\frac{|(2 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}+4 \\hat{k}) \\times((2-\\lambda) \\hat{i}+4 \\hat{k})|}{\\sqrt{29}}=\\frac{13}{\\sqrt{29}}\\right. \\\\ & |-8 \\hat{\\mathrm{j}}-3(2-\\lambda) \\hat{k}+12 \\hat{i}+4(2-\\lambda) \\hat{j}|=13 \\\\ & |12 \\hat{i}-4 \\lambda \\hat{j}+(3 \\lambda-6) \\hat{k}|=13\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & 144+16 \\lambda^2+(3 \\lambda-6)^2=169 \\\\ & 16 \\lambda^2+(3 \\lambda-6)^2=25=\\lambda \\Rightarrow=1\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
